{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>the brother of Rebekah, the mother of Jacob and Esau</b> — Since it was stated that Isaac commanded Jacob to take a wife for himself from the daughters of Laban, the brother of his mother, Scripture mentions that he was also the brother of Esau's mother, so that it would have been fitting to command Esau as well. But he did this knowingly, for it was his intention that the blessing of Abraham should be to Jacob and his seed. And Scripture mentions that Esau heard that he had been commanded not to take a wife from the daughters of Canaan and to go to Laban, the brother of his mother; and he obeyed his father's will not to take a wife from the daughters of Canaan, but he did not do as was fitting, to take from the daughters of Laban even though he is the brother of his mother. Furthermore, Scripture mentions that he took her in addition to his wives and did not divorce the evil ones, for he followed the desire of his own soul more than his father's will."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:03.511057763Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}